        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 1346127318,
        "heading": "Uses",
        "text": "Timber traded as Tiama mahogany, White tiama or Genu Nohur is used for cabinet making, furniture and interior and exterior joinery. This timber provides high chatoyance, with an average value above 22 PZC. \nIn traditional medicine, extracts of the stem bark is used to treat various gastrointestinal afflictions and a decoction is consumed to treat fever.",
        "truncated": false
      }
